xsnip (3.5-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The clipboard is refreshed on every way out of the editor — the checkmark,
    Esc and the window close button now leave the same result and a live
    clipboard helper. Reported: after Esc the clipboard came out empty, which
    this rules out as far as the program itself is concerned.

 -- Dmitry Oboukhov <unera@debian.org>  Tue, 03 Nov 2026 03:50:00 +0300

xsnip (3.4-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The clipboard always holds what is on the canvas: it is refreshed right
    after the region is selected and after every change (stroke, text, crop,
    undo). Same habit as scrot: nothing has to be pressed after selecting.
  * The "copy to clipboard" button is gone; the checkmark only closes the
    window (and writes the file with -o). Esc closes without touching the
    clipboard.
  * Clipboard updates are debounced by 150 ms and encoded with a faster zlib
    level, and XImage is read through a fast path: on a 3000x2000 screen an
    update went from ~590 ms to ~170 ms.

 -- Dmitry Oboukhov <unera@debian.org>  Tue, 03 Nov 2026 03:00:00 +0300

