xsnip (3.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Security: no more system("mkdir -p ...") built from XDG_CONFIG_HOME —
    the directory is created with mkdir(2), so a crafted XDG_CONFIG_HOME can
    no longer run commands (found by a code review, reproduced before the fix).
  * Build: the GUI test target is no longer called "check", so dh_auto_test
    does not run a screenshot test without a display; the package builds in a
    clean chroot again.
  * Clipboard: the INCR transfer restores the requestor's event mask, keeps up
    to four concurrent transfers and drops a stuck one after 30 seconds.
  * Numbers from the command line, config and --delay are parsed with the C
    locale: in ru_RU "--pen 2.5" used to be read as 2.
  * The toolbar scale is also capped by the widest monitor, so on a portrait
    screen the buttons stay inside the window.
  * Crop: the XOR rectangle is always erased, including the early return when
    the selection is too small.
  * Backspace deletes a whole UTF-8 character, not a byte.
  * The font cache no longer leaks XftFont objects when it is full; X errors
    are reported to stderr instead of being swallowed.
  * img_crop clamps its own coordinates; text insertion point is clamped too.
  * Cleanups: dead globals and atoms removed, XUnloadFont, correct version in
    --version and in the man page, Homepage/Source point at GitHub.

 -- Dmitry Oboukhov <unera@debian.org>  Tue, 03 Nov 2026 00:40:00 +0300

xsnip (3.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Resizing the editor window is fast now: while the size keeps changing only
    the toolbar is redrawn and the canvas is filled with grey, and the scaled
    image is rebuilt once, 120 ms after the last change. Before, every
    configure event re-ran the bilinear rescale of the whole image.

 -- Dmitry Oboukhov <unera@debian.org>  Mon, 02 Nov 2026 23:50:00 +0300

xsnip (2.9-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The toolbar scales with the tallest monitor: base is 800 points of height,
    so on a 1200-high screen the panel, its font and the icons are 1.5x
    bigger. Left at the old size on small screens.
  * Shortcut letters are no longer printed on the buttons; they are shown in
    the tooltips instead ("Pen (p)").

 -- Dmitry Oboukhov <unera@debian.org>  Mon, 02 Nov 2026 23:10:00 +0300

xsnip (2.8-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Tooltips: after 0.7 s of hovering over a button a small hint appears with
    its name (own override-redirect window, the image is not repainted).
  * Localisation without gettext: English (default), Russian and Chinese for
    the toolbar, tooltips and --help. The language comes from XSNIP_LANG,
    LC_ALL, LC_MESSAGES or LANG.
  * Fonts are chosen through fontconfig for the language, and text is drawn
    per character with fallback, so Chinese renders even though the default
    font has no CJK glyphs.
  * The undo icon is now a counter-clockwise arrow, as usual for undo.

 -- Dmitry Oboukhov <unera@debian.org>  Mon, 02 Nov 2026 22:30:00 +0300

xsnip (2.7-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Keyboard shortcuts no longer depend on the keyboard layout: they are
    matched by physical key (keysym of group 0), so p/t/r and Ctrl+Z work on
    a Russian layout too, where the same keys produce Cyrillic_pe and
    Cyrillic_ya. Text input through XIM is untouched.

 -- Dmitry Oboukhov <unera@debian.org>  Mon, 02 Nov 2026 21:45:00 +0300

xsnip (2.6-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The text input field is now sized from the tallest monitor: its font is
    monitor height / 25 (48 px on a 1200-pixel screen) instead of a fixed
    14 px. On a small screen the field used to be unreadable while the
    resulting text was fine; the size of text placed on the image is
    unchanged.

 -- Dmitry Oboukhov <unera@debian.org>  Mon, 02 Nov 2026 21:10:00 +0300

xsnip (2.5-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Tool shortcuts are now letters: p (pen), t (text), r (crop); the digit
    keys 1/2/3 keep working.
  * Cursors: pencil for the pen, I-beam for text, crosshair for crop; the
    crop tool used to show the text cursor.
  * Fix: the clipboard and done buttons were appended to the button list from
    inside the paint routine, so every repaint added two more entries, the
    32-slot array overflowed and the size buttons started reading garbage
    (that is why the minus/plus layout looked broken).

 -- Dmitry Oboukhov <unera@debian.org>  Mon, 02 Nov 2026 20:30:00 +0300

xsnip (2.4-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Region selection is fast now: the rectangle is a XOR rubber band and the
    dimmed background is painted once, the sharpened selection is shown only
    after the mouse stops (120 ms idle). Previously every mouse motion
    re-uploaded the whole screen image to the X server.
  * Excess motion events are coalesced in the selector too.
  * Fix: the minus/plus size buttons were drawn as "icon + label" although
    they have no icon, so the text was pushed to the right and the button
    looked broken.

 -- Dmitry Oboukhov <unera@debian.org>  Mon, 02 Nov 2026 19:55:00 +0300

xsnip (2.3-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Crop is fast now: the selection rectangle is drawn and erased with XOR
    instead of repainting the whole canvas on every mouse motion; excess
    motion events are coalesced. A 200-step drag takes well under a second
    where it used to take tens of seconds.
  * Crop works with two clicks as well: the first click sets a corner, the
    second one the opposite corner (dragging still works).
  * Undo (button and Ctrl+Z) covers cropping: it restores the previous image
    size and shifts the annotations back.

 -- Dmitry Oboukhov <unera@debian.org>  Mon, 02 Nov 2026 19:05:00 +0300

xsnip (2.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Toolbar rework: icons drawn with Xlib primitives, no image files.
    Undo button (counter-clockwise arrow) on the left, clipboard and done
    buttons on the right as icons, pen/text/crop with icon plus label.
  * New "crop" tool: drag a rectangle in the editor and the image is cut down
    to it, saved strokes follow the offset, then the pen is selected again.
  * Tool shortcut keys are now 1/2/3 for pen/text/crop, 4..8 for the palette.
  * The "close without saving" button is gone: Esc and the window close
    button do that.
  * Fix: double free of the image after cropping.

 -- Dmitry Oboukhov <unera@debian.org>  Mon, 02 Nov 2026 18:20:00 +0300

xsnip (2.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Multi-monitor support through Xinerama: without -s the screen under the
    pointer is grabbed, after -s the screen where the selection was made; the
    new -a/--all takes the whole virtual screen.
  * The editor window is bounded by its own screen and positioned relative to
    it, so it no longer straddles two monitors.
  * New "cancel" button: close without saving.
  * Text input now shows a caret at the insertion point, sized as the font.
  * Fix: strokes jumped up by the toolbar height when the mouse was released
    (the panel offset was missing when repainting saved operations).
  * Fix: the drawing cursor was shown over the toolbar.

 -- Dmitry Oboukhov <unera@debian.org>  Mon, 02 Nov 2026 17:10:00 +0300

xsnip (2.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release.
  * Screenshot of the whole screen or a mouse-selected region.
  * Minimal editor: pen and text, sizes in percent of min(width, height).
  * Five-colour palette, configurable via --colors and chosen with --color.
  * Settings (colour, sizes, tool, window type and position) persist in
    $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/xsnip/config.
  * --window dialog|normal and --pos center|tl|tr|bl|br for tiling WMs.
  * Clipboard is served by a forked X11 selection owner (PNG, INCR for
    large images), so the data survives the process exit.

 -- Dmitry Oboukhov <unera@debian.org>  Mon, 02 Nov 2026 17:00:00 +0300
